# Runtime target env for spring-on-exeris — Spring MVC + JPA running on the Exeris
# ingress in COMPATIBILITY mode (targets/exeris-spring-runtime-app-comp). Structural
# sibling of spring-runtime.env; the intended differences:
#
#   - Runner jar = the compat module's spring-benchmark-app jar, which boots the Exeris
#     kernel HTTP ingress + ExerisCompatDispatcher (ADR-011) instead of Tomcat. Same
#     Spring @RestController code, hosted on the Exeris runtime.
#   - Self-set port via EXERIS_PORT (app.properties maps exeris.runtime.network.port from
#     ${EXERIS_PORT}). Default moved 9004 -> 9018 on 2026-08-21: 9004 is restate's k6-facing
#     facade port and the saga roster runs both arms in one campaign. Health probe = :9018.
#   - JVM opts: SPRING_JAVA_OPTS carries the triad's iso-2048 Spring heap (1280m) + the
#     telemetry-off JFR overlay + NMT — IDENTICAL to spring-hibernate, so the
#     spring-hibernate vs spring-on-exeris pair is heap/diagnostics-fair (only the ingress
#     differs: Tomcat vs Exeris-compat). PLUS the embedded Exeris kernel's required
#     native-access flags (--add-opens sun.nio.ch/java.io, --enable-native-access) that it
#     needs. --enable-preview and -Dspring.classformat.ignore=true were dropped at
#     exeris-spring-runtime 0.7.0 (see below).
#
# LABELLING (corrected 2026-08-20): this is a COMPATIBILITY target, which is a SEPARATION
# AXIS, not a confidentiality boundary. Rows must be labelled Community + Compatibility + H1,
# stored separately, and routed to the compat/ track; they must never be blended with
# pure-mode rows (native Exeris / Tomcat Spring / Quarkus) without the explicit compat caveat.
# They are PUBLISHABLE.
#
# This comment previously read "EXCLUDED from the public docs path ... published
# internal-only", citing CLAUDE.md's Enterprise-vs-public scoping. That is the exact
# over-application CLAUDE.md now calls out by name: spring-on-exeris is NOT excluded
# (corrected 2026-08-11), exeris-spring-runtime is a product repo listed separately from the
# enterprise repos and has never been confidential, and every spring-on-exeris* arm is
# tier=community in the pair manifest. The confidentiality rule covers raw JFR/diagnostics
# and Enterprise internals (H3, locality, enterprise targets) — not open-core arms that
# happen to sit on a labelling axis whose neighbour is Enterprise. CLAUDE.md records this
# same conflation happening twice before; this file was a third instance.

START_MODE=external
HEALTH_URL=http://localhost:9018/health
HEALTH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=90

EXERIS_DB_JDBC_URL=${EXERIS_DB_JDBC_URL:-jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/postgres?prepareThreshold=1}
EXERIS_DB_USERNAME=${EXERIS_DB_USERNAME:-postgres}
EXERIS_DB_PASSWORD=${EXERIS_DB_PASSWORD:-postgres}
# Roster default is 32, matching every other saga arm. It was 256 here, inherited from the
# entity-read triad, and a pool eight times larger than every other arm is not a fair row.
EXERIS_DB_POOL_MIN_SIZE=${EXERIS_DB_POOL_MIN_SIZE:-16}
EXERIS_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE=${EXERIS_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE:-32}
SPRING_ON_EXERIS_PORT=${SPRING_ON_EXERIS_PORT:-9018}
SERVER_CPU_AFFINITY=${SERVER_CPU_AFFINITY:-}
SPRING_JAVA_OPTS=${SPRING_JAVA_OPTS:-}
EXERIS_AXONSERVER_HOST=${EXERIS_AXONSERVER_HOST:-localhost}
EXERIS_AXONSERVER_PORT=${EXERIS_AXONSERVER_PORT:-8124}
# Native-access flags the embedded Exeris kernel needs. --enable-preview and
# -Dspring.classformat.ignore=true were dropped 2026-08-21: they existed because the old kernel
# line shipped preview-marked classes (minor 0xFFFF) that Spring's classpath scan choked on.
# exeris-spring-runtime 0.7.0 pulls kernel 0.11.0 transitively (verified in the built jar), the
# same line exeris-community runs, and that line is not preview-marked. Appended AFTER
# SPRING_JAVA_OPTS so heap/JFR settings win.
EXERIS_NATIVE_JAVA_OPTS=${EXERIS_NATIVE_JAVA_OPTS:-'--add-opens java.base/sun.nio.ch=ALL-UNNAMED --add-opens java.base/java.io=ALL-UNNAMED --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED'}
EXTERNAL_PID_FILE=${EXTERNAL_PID_FILE:-/tmp/exeris-${USER:-unknown}-spring-on-exeris.pid}

EXTERNAL_START_CMD='EXERIS_PORT="$SPRING_ON_EXERIS_PORT" EXERIS_HTTP_MAX_VERSION="${EXERIS_HTTP_MAX_VERSION:-HTTP_1_1}" EXERIS_HTTP_H2C_UPGRADE_ENABLED="${EXERIS_HTTP_H2C_UPGRADE_ENABLED:-false}" EXERIS_DB_JDBC_URL="$EXERIS_DB_JDBC_URL" EXERIS_DB_USERNAME="$EXERIS_DB_USERNAME" EXERIS_DB_PASSWORD="$EXERIS_DB_PASSWORD" EXERIS_DB_POOL_MIN_SIZE="$EXERIS_DB_POOL_MIN_SIZE" EXERIS_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE="$EXERIS_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE" SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL="$EXERIS_DB_JDBC_URL" SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME="$EXERIS_DB_USERNAME" SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD="$EXERIS_DB_PASSWORD" SPRING_DATASOURCE_HIKARI_MINIMUM_IDLE="$EXERIS_DB_POOL_MIN_SIZE" SPRING_DATASOURCE_HIKARI_MAXIMUM_POOL_SIZE="$EXERIS_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE" EXERIS_AXONSERVER_HOST="$EXERIS_AXONSERVER_HOST" EXERIS_AXONSERVER_PORT="$EXERIS_AXONSERVER_PORT" ${SERVER_CPU_AFFINITY:+taskset -c ${SERVER_CPU_AFFINITY} }java $SPRING_JAVA_OPTS $EXERIS_NATIVE_JAVA_OPTS -jar targets/exeris-spring-runtime-app-comp/target/spring-benchmark-app-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar > /tmp/exeris-spring-on-exeris-${SPRING_ON_EXERIS_PORT}.log 2>&1 & echo $! > "$EXTERNAL_PID_FILE"'
EXTERNAL_STOP_CMD='if [[ -f "$EXTERNAL_PID_FILE" ]]; then pid="$(cat "$EXTERNAL_PID_FILE")"; kill "$pid" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; rm -f "$EXTERNAL_PID_FILE"; fi'

TARGET_TIER=community
TARGET_PROTOCOL=h1
COMPARISON_AXIS=within-tier-compat

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAGA ROSTER (e2e-shop-order-saga, CONTRACT-v2.2, added 2026-08-20)
#
# This env was written for the entity-read triad, where the arm co-resides with
# spring-hibernate. Three things had to be reconciled before it could serve as a saga roster
# arm under spring_on_exeris_h1_park100_v3, and none of them was a version bump. All three are
# now closed — by measurement, not assumption:
#
#   1. PORT COLLISION — RESOLVED 2026-08-21. 9004 is also restate's k6-facing facade port
#      (runtime/drivers/env/restate-runtime.env), and the saga campaign runs both arms in one
#      roster. spring-on-exeris is the newcomer, so it moved to 9018, which the asset matrix
#      confirms nothing else claims.
#
#   2. POOL SIZE — RESOLVED 2026-08-21. The default here was 256, inherited from the
#      entity-read triad, against the saga roster's 32. A pool eight times larger than every
#      other arm's is not a fair row. The default is now 32; the runner still exports the
#      roster value on top of it.
#
#   3. --enable-preview — RESOLVED 2026-08-21, by reading the built jar rather than assuming
#      in either direction. exeris-spring-runtime 0.7.0 pulls exeris-kernel-{core,spi,community}
#      0.11.0 transitively — the SAME line exeris-community runs, which also removes what would
#      otherwise have been a fairness problem inside the Exeris family, two arms on two kernel
#      lines. 0.11.0 is not preview-marked, so --enable-preview and
#      -Dspring.classformat.ignore=true are gone here exactly as they are on exeris-community.
#
# SAGA ELIGIBILITY REMAINS THE OPEN QUESTION, AND IT IS NOT THE VERSION. The asset matrix
# recorded, against 0.5.0-SNAPSHOT, that this arm's saga terminal state does not resolve at all:
# flow steps run on kernel worker virtual threads outside the request-scoped compat provider
# binding, giving saga_success_rate=0. That is the same family of defect as the storage-context
# scope mismatch fixed in exeris-community on 2026-08-19, and 0.7.0 now carries kernel 0.11.0 -
# so the old verdict cannot be carried forward unexamined in EITHER direction: not as "still
# broken", and not as "surely fixed by the bump". It has to be re-measured.
#
# Until a run under spring_on_exeris_h1_park100_v3 resolves its sagas, the arm is "listed and
# pending" per CONTRACT-v2.2 §1 — it does not silently disappear from the roster table, and it
# does not appear in it as a measured row either.
